lines+=['', 'Fast retrieval indexes every sixth map ORB descriptor and queries every fourth, rather than every third and every second. It does NOT change depth geometry, RANSAC thresholds, or mapping poses. CPU time is from the offline process; no ROS/Jetson end-to-end FPS guarantee.', '', '## Required upgrades (ordered)','', '1. **Keep the coarse image-retrieval + geometric-verification architecture** but add a proper visual place recognition global embedding/retrieval index (e.g. CosPlace/EigenPlaces/AnyLoc) and benchmark on these SAME held-out bags; use a vocabulary/global retrieval layer to avoid matching against every keyframe.', '2. **Improve local feature robustness:** benchmark learned lightweight XFeat (and optionally XFeat+LighterGlue) against ORB, particularly repeated trees, low-light, shade, reflections and camera motion. Do not mix incompatible descriptor types; rebuild map descriptor cache and query frontend together.', '3. **Improve the map itself:** track correspondences across keyframes, merge repeated 3D points, reject dynamic objects (pedestrians/vehicles, windblown foliage), add structure coverage metrics, depth-confidence limits and multi-view bundle adjustment. Loop-close shared LiDAR/visual trajectory and physically verify LiDAR–IMU/base.', '4. **Temporal LiDAR–camera multi-hypothesis:** store several visual PnP/LiDAR GICP poses, enforce 2–3 image/scan confirmations plus locally consistent motion over timestamps, use the independently observed branch to rank hypotheses. Global authority must signal AMBIGUOUS/UNTRUSTED on large disagreement and withhold a navigation pose.', '5. **For LiDAR-failure fallback:** extend current `fresh_visual_global_localizer.py`, which is local search/GPS fallback-only, to support cold GPS-free global image retrieval; bound CPU with query throttling, worker queue, stale-image dropping, monitored per-stage timings, and delayed timestamp-correct map update. Add real ROS1 bag replay end-to-end integration and tests.', '', '## Critical limitations','', '- Current result is an **offline global visual candidate benchmark** and a newly built map, not a validated streaming visual global pose authority.', '- Registered depth errors, LiDAR-map trajectory drift, camera/IMU physical extrinsic errors, and limited surveyed landmarks may corrupt metric poses even when PnP reprojection is low.', '- Source map uses a 225s unoptimized LiDAR-only trajectory, not the questionable 3,130-pose camera-fused full trajectory, and not a loop-closed map.', '- No GPS was used in map construction retrieval or evaluation. Baseline cold retrieval contains NO spatial pose priors.', '- `outputs/visual_global_20261020/feature_coverage.png`, `visual_keyframes_contact_sheet.jpg`, and `visual/landmarks_preview.pcd` illustrate the database. `visual_relocalization_timelines.png` and `visual_vs_lidar_branch_localization3.png` show held-out results.', '', '## Reproducibility','', 'See `scripts/build_full_visual_rgbd_map.py`, `scripts/benchmark_visual_global_rgbd.py`, `scripts/report_visual_rgbd_global_20261020.py`; source bags and map were read-only, and production `/pose` untouched.']
